@startuml
title SIC/XE Language Server - Document and Editor Request Sequence
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false

actor Developer
participant "Monaco (CodeEditor)" as Editor
participant "AssemblerLanguageClient" as Client
participant "WebSocket /language" as WS
participant "Server language WebSocket handler" as Server
participant "AssemblerLanguageSession\n(per connection)" as Session
participant "sicxe::Assembler" as Assembler

note over Session
Each WebSocket connection gets its own session.
The session stores open documents, versions, and cached analysis results.
end note

== Connect and initialize ==
Editor -> Client: start()
Client -> WS: Open WebSocket
WS -> Server: Accept connection
Server -> Session: Create session
Client -> WS: initialize request
WS -> Session: handle(initialize)
Session --> WS: Capabilities and SIC/XE vocabulary
WS --> Client: initialize response with request id
Client -> WS: initialized notification
WS -> Session: handle(initialized)
Client --> Editor: Publish language catalog

== Open source document ==
Developer -> Editor: Open SIC/XE source
Editor -> Client: openDocument(uri, text)
Client -> WS: textDocument/didOpen\n(uri, languageId, version, text)
WS -> Session: handle(didOpen)
Session -> Session: Store document and version
Session -> Session: Analyze document when needed
Session -> Assembler: assembleDetailed(text)
Assembler --> Session: AssemblyResult and diagnostics
Session -> Session: Map assembler diagnostics to LSP ranges
Session --> WS: textDocument/publishDiagnostics\n(uri, version, diagnostics)
WS --> Client: Diagnostics notification
Client --> Editor: Set Monaco markers

== Edit and synchronize ==
Developer -> Editor: Edit source text
Editor -> Client: changeDocument(uri, text)
note right of Client
Client increments the version and debounces
full-text updates for 250 ms.
end note
... debounce interval ...
Client -> WS: textDocument/didChange\n(version, full document text)
WS -> Session: handle(didChange)
Session -> Session: Ignore stale version; replace text;\nmark unsaved and unanalyzed
Session -> Assembler: assembleDetailed(updated text)
Assembler --> Session: Updated AssemblyResult
Session -> Session: Publish diagnostics for this version
Session --> WS: textDocument/publishDiagnostics
WS --> Client: Diagnostics notification
Client --> Editor: Ignore stale diagnostics; update markers

== Language feature request ==
Developer -> Editor: Request completion, hover, definition,\nreferences, or rename
Editor -> Client: request(method, params)
Client -> WS: JSON-RPC request\n(method, document URI, position)
WS -> Session: handle(request)
Session -> Session: Find document; analyze if cache is stale
Session -> Assembler: assembleDetailed(text)\n(only if analysis is stale)
Assembler --> Session: AssemblyResult
Session -> Session: Compute feature result from document\nand assembly metadata
Session --> WS: JSON-RPC result or error\n(matching request id)
WS --> Client: Result or error
Client --> Editor: Resolve Monaco provider request

== Save and close ==
Developer -> Editor: Save or close source file
Editor -> Client: saveDocument(uri, text)
Client -> WS: textDocument/didSave
WS -> Session: Mark saved and analyze
Session --> WS: publishDiagnostics\n(including save-time missing END warning)
WS --> Client: Diagnostics notification
Client --> Editor: Update markers
Editor -> Client: closeDocument(uri)
Client -> WS: textDocument/didClose
WS -> Session: Erase document
Session --> WS: publishDiagnostics(uri, [])
WS --> Client: Clear diagnostics notification

note over Client,Session
didOpen, didChange, didSave, and didClose are notifications and have no
JSON-RPC response. initialize and language feature calls are requests and
return a response with the matching id. Invalid JSON is rejected by the
WebSocket handler with a parse error before session dispatch.
end note

note over Session,Assembler
The language service uses the assembler library for source analysis.
It does not load a project into the Simulator or mutate memory,
registers, or execution history.
end note
@enduml
